	abstract = {We describe ongoing searches for intermediate-mass black holes with MBH≈ 100 − 105 M . We review a range of search mechanisms, both dynamical and those that rely on accretion signatures. We ﬁnd: • Dynamical and accretion signatures alike point to a high fraction of 109 − 1010 M galaxies hosting black holes with MBH ∼ 105 M . In contrast, there are no solid detections of black holes in globular clusters. • There are few observational constraints on black holes in any environment with MBH ≈ 100 − 104 M .},
